    "goal": "D",
    "status": "Completed the requested experiment; whole-closure A-24 remains open on observed differences.",
    "implementation_commit": "864c63794d055cea0622082a69b5c51e1497aabe",
    "scope": "SYNTH-1 deletion of one scripted confirmed exemplar, actual deterministic byte regeneration, and two fresh CPU pose executions over a synthetic multiview room. No personal media, model endpoint or production deployment.",
    "decisions": [
      {
        "number": 1,
        "name": "Only independently observed content is claimed identical",
        "adr": "docs/adr/0021-observed-recomputation-scope.md",
        "invariant": "The exemplar payload and dependencies rebuilt after deletion must equal a baseline created before the deleted source existed. Stored payloads must agree with their canonical key. Recomputing intake and rendition means evicting their bytes and verifying absence before the real stages run. No model-backed exactness claim is permitted.",
        "rationale": "A cache hit and a deterministic flag are insufficient evidence of recomputation. Append-only history and derived aggregate metadata can differ even when the canonical surviving exemplars reproduce. The brief explicitly accepts retained mismatches; claiming whole-state equality would contradict the observed graph and pose receipts.",
        "canonical_representation": "Strict canonical_json of identity-match-context/v1 payload and typed graph projections; raw SHA-256 of actual artifact bytes; existing float-bearing colmap-pose-receipt/v2 retained as exact separate artifacts. The envelope carries only integer-safe values and hashes. Nothing is rounded to create equality.",
        "compatibility_impact": "Adds IntegrityError refusal for a live stored exemplar payload that disagrees with its content-derived key. No schema migration, stage identity, API or browser shape changes. Historical stale generations remain stale.",
        "failure_behaviour": "Deleted inputs are excluded and a corrupt index raises. Nondeterministic rendition output fails the experiment and the existing deterministic writer flags repair. Real scene and pose mismatches are retained and block broad exactness claims; the experiment does not assert that current aggregate defects are desirable behaviour.",
